hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19638","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from al-Hajjaj, meaning al-Sawwaf ibn Abi Uthman, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah and Abu Salamah from Abu Qatadah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with us and recite in Dhuhr and Asr, in the first two units, the Opening of the Book and two surahs, and would let us hear a verse sometimes. He would lengthen the first unit of Dhuhr and shorten the second, and likewise in the dawn prayer."
"19639","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you drinks, let him not breathe into the vessel, and when he enters the privy, let him not wipe himself with his right hand, and when he urinates, let him not touch his private part with his right hand."
"19640","Yahya ibn Abi Kathir said: Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him not eat with his left hand, and when he drinks, let him not drink with his left hand, and when he takes, let him not take with his left hand, and when he gives, let him not give with his left hand."
